# The words of the window of FreeSynergy Resources, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
app-name = FreeSynergy Resources
app-tagline = Goal: Know what we have and what we need: things, rooms and material, who may use them when, and who offers what. Two people cannot book the same room by accident.
soon = coming soon
state-connected = The server answers and speaks the contract {$contract}.
state-down = No server is running: {$reason}
state-contract = This frontend does not fit the server: {$reason}
state-hint-down = Start the program with the command `fs-resources`; it starts the server and this window.
state-hint-contract = Install a matching version of FreeSynergy Resources; the window below only shows what is planned.
today-title = What it can do today
today-1 = Opens this window, finds its server (`fs-resources serve`) and checks that both speak the same contract version. The server names what it offers (nothing yet) and answers nothing else.
today-2 = Says plainly what is not there yet: nothing in this window can be used to manage things yet.
today-3 = The core (things, rooms, material, reservations that cannot overbook, free time, needs and offers, your own capacity) exists as a library and is not connected to this window yet. The server keeps running after the window is closed.
coming-title = What comes
coming-1 = Things, rooms and material: a list with search and filter, create, change, archive. Deleting is refused with the reason while a reservation is confirmed.
coming-2 = Reserve: pick a thing, a period and a quantity; an overbooking is refused and the reason is shown.
coming-3 = Availability: a strip of free and busy time for one thing over a period.
coming-4 = Confirm, change, cancel and finish a reservation (give back, or use up material); the stock of material is shown and can be corrected.
coming-5 = Needs and offers in one form: someone posts a need, someone makes an offer, and accepting the offer makes the reservation.
coming-6 = Keyboard: arrows in lists, Del, F2, Ctrl+N; columns and sorting.
coming-7 = Your own time (capacity and sharing with a group, with the limits shown): only once the server knows who is asking. Planned, not scheduled.
coming-8 = Recast on the ValueFlows model (kind of thing with a typed unit, hand-over, commitment, catalogue as a filter), together with typed storage. Planned, not scheduled. A marketplace would later be a facet on offers and needs, not a program of its own.
menu-program = Resources
menu-new = New thing or room
menu-reserve = Reserve
menu-search = Search
menu-chosen = Chosen: {$entry}
screen-start = Start
screen-comes = What comes
status-ready = Ready
